questions.question:
The "My courses" page loads like this:

let courses;
try {
  const res = await fetch("https://api.codedev.test/me/enrollments");
  courses = await res.json();
} catch {
  courses = [];
}
render(courses.length ? courseList(courses) : "You have no courses yet");

Network tab:
GET /me/enrollments  503  application/json
Response: {"error":"service_unavailable"}

Statement: "For this response, the catch block runs and sets courses to an empty array."

The course search box sends a request on every keystroke and renders each response when it arrives:

input.addEventListener("input", async () => {
  const res = await fetch(`https://api.codedev.test/courses?q=${encodeURIComponent(input.value)}`);
  renderResults(await res.json());
});

A learner types "p" and then "y". Network tab, in start order:

GET /courses?q=p    200   940 ms
GET /courses?q=py   200   180 ms

Statement: "The list can end up showing the results for \"p\" while the search box shows \"py\"."
